    while playing in the Editor on Quest Link when the Game view was not focused.
    ([UUM-139424](https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/product/unity/issues/guid/UUM-139424))\n-
    Fixed issue in `OneEuroFilterVector3` where speeds were occasionally negative
    which would cause unexpected behavior when resetting the hands in the `XRDeviceSimulator`.
    ([UUM-139967](https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/product/unity/issues/guid/UUM-139967))\n-
    Fixed error from exception \"ObjectDisposedException: The Unity.Collections.NativeArray`1[UnityEngine.XR.Hands.XRHandJoint]
    has been deallocated, it is not allowed to access it\" when exiting Play mode
    in the Hands Interaction Demo sample by updating sample scripts to check that
    the XRHandSubsystem is still running.\n- Fixed `XRMousePointer` in XR Mouse Interaction
    Demo sample to remove hover event listeners on destroy.\n- Fixed `ToggleColorToggler`
    component in the Starter Assets sample to initialize the colors of the Toggle
    component during `OnEnable` to ensure the Toggle is in the correct color state
    to fix implicit ordering dependency with other scripts.\n- Fixed unhandled division
    by zero in `CurveVisualController`. ([UUM-141267](https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/product/unity/issues/guid/UUM-141267))\n-
    Fixed issue where the `XRUIInputModule` component is automatically added to an
    Event System GameObject, but does not check for existing `BaseInputModule`-based
    components that would interfere with how XRI interacts with the Event System,
    such as the `InputSystemUIInputModule`. XRI will now log a warning and disable
    the other Input Modules. [UUM-137143](https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/product/unity/issues/guid/UUM-137143)\n-
    Fixed inverted logic for One Euro Filter in `OneEuroFilterVector3`."}'
