  upmReserved: "{\"changelog\":\"### Fixed\\n- Fix error while verifying module from
    invalid bitcast when converting nunit to float or double.\\n- Fixed cases where
    the Burst Inspector could jitter when moving the divider.\\n- Fixed that using
    a Bursted function pointer as argument to a method directly could cause a compiler
    error\\n- Fixed Burst AOT builds for Embedded Linux and QNX when using Build
    Profiles: Burst now reads the active profile\u2019s architecture instead of a
    stale editor setting, preventing sysroot/linker failures (e.g. x64 SDK with aarch64
    target) in batchmode and CI.\\n- Atomics were not generated when target web platform
    with threading enabled.\\n- Fixed a race between Burst and the Editor compilation
    pipeline that could surface as a `Failed to find entry-points` error.\\n- Burst
    could crash if Very Large static readonly data happened to be compiled in such
    a way that it would result in a direct store of the array. Now, the very large
    data is memmoved instead.\\n- Web Player would crash if targeting wasm and the
    entities package is present.\\n- Very large constants could cause Burst to crash
    when compiling for WebAssembly\\n\\n### Changed\\n- Changed the default LLVM
    version to 21.\\n- The minimum required Linux version to use Burst in the Unity
    Editor is now Ubuntu 18.04 or equivalent.\\n- Changed minimum Editor version
    to 6.0\\n- `[IgnoreWarning(1371)]` applied to a `[BurstDiscard]` method now suppresses
    the discarded-call warning for the calls discarded along with it, instead of
    having to annotate every caller.\\n\\n### Removed\\n- Removed support for LLVM
    10, 15, 16, 17.\\n\\n### Known Issues\\n- Windows Smart App Control or WDAC policies
    may block JIT-compiled libraries at load time. Burst now logs a warning in such
    cases and deletes the affected library, which will be recompiled so Burst can
    attempt loading it again.\\n\\n### Added\\n- Support for Wasm64 target\\n- Added
    `ButtonFlowNewLineTest` editor test to verify that the Burst Inspector button
    bar wraps to a new line when the window is narrow, and fits on a single line
    when the window is wide.\\n- Added a Restart Now button to the dialog shown when
    the Burst package is removed or updated.\"}"
